#: inc/customizer/callbacks/about-country.php:172
msgid ""
"The population of Nepal was recorded to be about 26.62 million according to "
"a recent survey done by the Central Bureau of Statistics, Nepal. The "
"population comprises of about a 101 ethnic groups speaking over 92 languages."
" The distinction in caste and ethnicity is understood more easily with a "
"view of customary layout of the population. Though, there exist numerous "
"dialects, the language of unification is the national language, Nepali. "
"Nepali is the official language of the state, spoken and understood by "
"majority of the population. Multiple ethnic groups have their own mother "
"tongues. English is spoken by many in Government and business offices. It is "
"the mode of education in most private schools of Kathmandu and some other "
"cities."
